---
# rendered per control into <ctl>/playbooks/probe_privileged_contact.yml (G). Controller-local fixture of lifecycle E73
# (control target.contact.privileged-trust-basis-declaration; codex 171945: built and executed before privileged-leg
# qualification). It runs the checkout's OWN resolve (tasks/resolve_policy.yml) and then its OWN
# tasks/initial_contact.yml in the PRIVILEGED variant, exactly as B's privileged plays include it, against ONE TEST-NET-1
# target (192.0.2.0/24, unroutable; act.yml refuses any other address). The checkout under test is the act's extra-var
# rhc_ic_checkout: the control's declared variant clone {vclone}, whose profile is the candidate + ONE declared patch.
# No root and no SSH binary: the play's ssh executable is the non-network stub below, so a raw task that is reached
# gets rc 1 with empty output (ansible-core 2.19.11 ssh.py raises a connection failure only on 255). The act traces
# connect + execve; its no_network judge covers only non-loopback AF_INET/AF_INET6 connect() (controls.j2 network_lines).
# The declaration assert ("Refuse a privileged tool declaration whose trust basis is not the declared partition") is
# controller-side and runs before INITIAL CONTACT 1, so a refused declaration never reaches a raw task. The unchanged
# declaration passes it; IC1 (failed_when: false) then records the stub's rc 1 and the FIRST failure is the post-IC1
# digest assert (non-vacuity). Generic: no variant-specific value is rendered.
# rh_repo_root is bound here from rhc_ic_checkout because this rendered playbook lives outside every checkout
# (refuse_pinned_outputs.yml derives it from playbook_dir); that first-entry guard is not what E73 tests.
- name: Privileged initial-contact declaration probe (E73 fixture; TEST-NET-1 target, stubbed ssh, no root)
  hosts: {{ rh.controller.bootstrap.inventory.target_group }}
  gather_facts: false
  become: false
  vars:
    ansible_ssh_executable: /usr/bin/false
  tasks:
{% raw %}
    - name: Bind the checkout under test (the control's variant clone; fixture binding, not an input of the route)
      ansible.builtin.set_fact:
        rh_repo_root: "{{ rhc_ic_checkout }}"

    - name: Resolve the harness policy of the checkout under test through its engine
      ansible.builtin.include_tasks: "{{ rh_repo_root }}/testing/remote_harness/tasks/resolve_policy.yml"

    - name: The route's PRIVILEGED INITIAL CONTACT of the checkout under test (raw only)
      ansible.builtin.include_tasks: "{{ rh_repo_root }}/testing/remote_harness/tasks/initial_contact.yml"
      vars:
        rh_ic_variant: privileged
        rh_ic_paths: [/srv/lme-rhc-e73]
{% endraw %}
